WEBVTT

1
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.800
...was so ably pointed out
by the Secretary-General

2
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.000
in his opening remarks.

3
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.800
But - and I must emphasise this point -

4
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.000
no formula can. or will.
ever cover each case.

5
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.500
For instance...

6
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.000
...when three or more applicants
have been recognised.

7
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.600
which is in direct contradiction to...

8
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.100
Whose funeral is it?

9
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.000
Yours.

10
00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.300
One more time again.

11
00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.900
Not married. by any chance. are you?

12
00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.300
Good morning. 007.

13
00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.400
Good... good morning.

14
00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.400
Insomnia. sir?

15
00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.100
Instructions.

16
00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:34.300
You haven't much time.
I'll explain as you pack.

17
00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.800
Pack. sir?

18
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.700
Three agents have been killed
in the last 24 hours.

19
00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.700
Dawes in New York. Hamilton in
New Orleans and Baines in the Caribbean.

20
00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:48.800
Baines. I rather liked Baines.
We shared the same boot maker.

21
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.600
Coffee.

22
00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:53.100
sir?

23
00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.900
I take it these killings are connected?

24
00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.700
That's precisely
what you're going to find out.

25
00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:21.500
Baines was working on a small
Caribbean island called San Monique.

26
00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.500
Dawes was in New York.
keeping an eye on its prime minister.

27
00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.800
one Dr Kananga.

28
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.700
Hamilton was on loan to the Americans
in New Orleans.

29
00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.300
Is that all it does?

30
00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.600
By the way. congratulations.

31
00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:45.700
The Italians were most impressed
by the way you handled the Rome affair.

32
00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.500
Thank you. sir.

33
00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:49.200
Sugar?

34
00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.700
Thanks.

35
00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.900
The authorities
were more than helpful.

36
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.200
There's one small complaint.

37
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.200
They seem to be missing
one of their agents.

38
00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.800
A Miss... Caruso.

39
00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:10.000
You wouldn't happen to know
where she is?

40
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.600
Miss Moneypenny.

41
00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:15.700
- Morning. Moneypenny.
- Good morning. sir.

42
00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:19.400
- It's only the hour that's indecent.
- Really?

43
00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:23.600
I've got your ticket to New York.
Q has repaired your wristwatch.

44
00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:27.700
- And some background on San Monique.
- Thank you. Moneypenny.

45
00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:32.000
I'm sure the overburdened British
taxpayer will be fascinated to know

46
00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:35.300
will how the Special Ordnance Section
disburses its funds.

47
00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:39.800
In future. Commander. may I suggest
a perfectly adequate watchmaker

48
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.900
just down the street.

49
00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.200
Good God!

50
00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:51.400
Pulling out this button turns the watch
into a hyper-intensified magnetic field.

51
00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.200
powerful enough to deflect
the path of a bullet

52
00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:59.700
- at long range - or so Q claims.
- I feel tempted to test that theory now.

53
00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:03.700
If you don't mind. Commander. my spoon.

54
00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.200
Sorry. sir.

55
00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.200
Thank you.

56
00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.700
Dr Kananga is at present in New York.

57
00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:13.900
The CIA have been informed.
They are helping with surveillance.

58
00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.300
Your flight arrives at 11.30am.

59
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.500
Now. where did I leave my coat?

60
00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.700
Allow me.

61
00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.300
Thank you.
Come along. Miss Moneypenny.

62
00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:31.800
- Morning. Bond.
- Sir.

63
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.000
Miss Moneypenny.

64
00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:36.500
Thank you.

65
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.800
Goodbye. James.

66
00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:44.900
Or should I say... ciao. bello?

67
00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:19.400
Such a delicate touch.

68
00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:22.500
Sheer magnetism. darling.

69
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.000
A man comes.

70
00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.300
He travels quickly.

71
00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.500
He has purpose.

72
00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.500
He comes over water.

73
00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.400
He travels with others.

74
00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.200
He will oppose.

75
00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.000
He brings violence and destruction.

76
00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.600
Hello.

77
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.400
- Mr Leiter for you. sir.
- Thank you.

78
00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:43.400
Hello. Felix. How are you?

79
00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:47.000
Traffic permitting.
I should be with you in half an hour.

80
00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:50.000
Then you can buy me
the best lunch in New York.

81
00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:53.500
Hi. James. Your friend Kananga
has just left the UN.

82
00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.200
He's probably headed back
to his embassy.

83
00:13:56.300 --> 00:14:00.700
No. don't worry. The place is eyeballed.
wired for sound - the works.

84
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.000
Right. I'll see you in a half-hour.

85
00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.100
Easy. Charlie.
Let's get there in one piece.

86
00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:03.300
Charlie?

87
00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.200
Right. stand by.

88
00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:52.300
Here comes Kananga's limousine.

89
00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.800
Out he gets

90
00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.000
with the usual goon squad

91
00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.200
and the girl.

92
00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:05.000
Time: 11.46.

93
00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.600
What is that?!

94
00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:17.700
Felix? You know I hate to trouble you.
but I've run into a little bother.

95
00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.300
You what?!

96
00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.600
Get me a make on a white pimp mobile.

97
00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.800
3-4-7. Nelson David George.

98
00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:36.800
It would seem. Dr Kananga.
that the conference has not

99
00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:38.600
lived up to your expectations.

100
00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.500
We can only hope that
this is a temporary setback.

101
00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.500
However. I do have
some observations to make.

102
00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.200
Take a letter. please.

103
00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:51.400
To Secretary-General.
Pan-Island Unity Conference.

104
00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:54.000
Sir...

105
00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:59.200
I wish to point out...

106
00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.600
that...

107
00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:04.800
too many
of our island neighbours

108
00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:09.500
have once again let themselves be...
bullied by United States industry.

109
00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.800
The story is an old one.

110
00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:14.200
the record a clear one.

111
00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:17.700
Since my historic statement of principles

112
00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:21.400
was delivered and acted upon
some six months ago.

113
00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:25.200
our economic outlook
has improved dramatically.

114
00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:30.500
By exercising our policy of friendship
to all with favouritism towards none.

115
00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:34.000
new respect for the entire area
has been injected.

116
00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.000
And even though some of my...

117
00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:40.100
James? That car is registered
to a shop at 33 East 65th Street.

118
00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.200
That's only a block away from here.

119
00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:46.100
Right. Take your time. buddy.
Kananga's knitting a flag in there.

120
00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:48.700
It might be the easiest thing to do.

121
00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.900
Something... in heads?

122
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:19.300
Just browsing. thank you.

123
00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.400
Five dollars.

124
00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.700
Do you think you could
gift wrap it for me. please?

125
00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:51.000
Lengthwise. if you don't mind.

126
00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.800
Thank you.

127
00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:18.000
...remains my first concern.

128
00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:22.700
Thus San Monique's obligations to
her island neighbours would seem clear.

129
00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:26.000
Those who fawn and crawl
in the face of intimidation

130
00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:29.500
must perforce look up
to those who stand. proudly.

131
00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.200
wrapped in a justifiable self-confidence.

132
00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:36.500
The time has come.
painful as it may be.

133
00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:41.400
to gaze out among our sister nations
in the area and see if any stands...

134
00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:36.800
He's tailing.

135
00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:43.700
I got him in my sights.

136
00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:00.500
- You know where you're goin'. man?
- Uptown. I believe.

137
00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:04.300
Uptown? We headin' into Harlem. man.

138
00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:08.200
Just keep on the tail of that jukebox
and there's an extra $20 for you.

139
00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:13.300
Man. for 20 bucks.
I'd take you to a Ku Klux Klan cookout.

140
00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:33.500
1 25th. You got a honky on your tail.

141
00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:49.700
He's heading east.

142
00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:52.300
Can't miss him.
It's like following a cue ball.

143
00:21:57.600 --> 00:22:00.200
That's the car.
They must have gone inside.

144
00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:02.400
Pull up where you can.

145
00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:11.300
Sure hope you make friends easy.

146
00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:13.600
Right on. brother.

147
00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:18.900
He's headin' on in!

148
00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:45.900
Good afternoon.

149
00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:49.700
- Bourbon and water. please.
- The first booth will do.

150
00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:52.700
Tell him neat. would you?

151
00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:55.600
- No ice.
- That's extra. man.

152
00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:14.400
I'd like something on the side as well.

153
00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:16.300
Information.

154
00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:18.500
Three men and a girl came in...

155
00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:25.700
Relax. baby.

156
00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.200
Mr Big's gonna take care of you
in a minute.

157
00:23:51.300 --> 00:23:54.300
Black queen on the red king. Miss...?

158
00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:56.600
Solitaire.

159
00:23:56.800 --> 00:23:58.900
My name's Bond.

160
00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:01.900
James Bond.

161
00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.500
I know who you are.

162
00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:06.600
what you are. and why you've come.

163
00:24:06.700 --> 00:24:08.300
You've made a mistake.

164
00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:11.000
You will not succeed.

165
00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:14.700
Rather a sweeping statement.
considering we've never met.

166
00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:17.400
The cards have followed you for me.

167
00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:22.200
You get ripped off in Detroit.
you yell out to me! D'you hear?

168
00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:28.500
Is he armed?

169
00:24:30.900 --> 00:24:33.400
You can't be too careful in New York City.

170
00:24:57.000 --> 00:25:00.700
Funny how the least little thing
amuses him.

171
00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:08.900
Fascinating.

172
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:12.700
That's you. quite obviously.
An amazing resemblance.

173
00:25:12.900 --> 00:25:15.000
Am I in there as well?

174
00:25:16.300 --> 00:25:17.800
Pick a card.

175
00:25:21.400 --> 00:25:22.800
Turn it over.

176
00:25:25.800 --> 00:25:27.900
You have found yourself.

177
00:25:28.700 --> 00:25:32.200
I'm telling you.
go out to LA and clean it up

178
00:25:32.400 --> 00:25:35.900
or I'm coming out there
and clean you up. And I mean that!

179
00:25:36.600 --> 00:25:39.300
Is this the stupid mother
that tailed you uptown?

180
00:25:39.500 --> 00:25:42.700
There seems to be some mistake.
My name...

181
00:25:42.800 --> 00:25:44.800
Names is for tombstones. baby.

182
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:47.900
Y'all take this honky out
and waste him - now!

183
00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:56.000
- "Waste him"? Is that a good thing?
- The reading is over.

184
00:25:56.100 --> 00:25:58.100
Nothing about my future?

185
00:26:06.800 --> 00:26:08.200
Us?

186
00:26:12.100 --> 00:26:15.800
Now. promise you'll stay right there.
I shan't be long.

187
00:26:25.400 --> 00:26:26.700
Thank you.

188
00:26:44.800 --> 00:26:46.800
Keep your hands up. honky.

189
00:26:46.900 --> 00:26:49.900
What's he think this is?
Blow his friggin' head off.

190
00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:03.800
Drop it!

191
00:27:08.700 --> 00:27:10.300
Now.

192
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:21.700
Harold Strutter. CIA. Where were you
when I didn't need you?

193
00:27:21.800 --> 00:27:24.300
It got obvious
you weren't coming out front.

194
00:27:24.500 --> 00:27:27.600
Not even with that clever disguise
you were wearing.

195
00:27:27.700 --> 00:27:29.700
A white face in Harlem.

196
00:27:29.900 --> 00:27:32.600
Good thinking. Bond.
Let's get outta here.

197
00:27:36.600 --> 00:27:38.700
I'm surprised they didn't spot you.

198
00:27:38.800 --> 00:27:42.200
There's a remarkable girl back there
with a deck of cards.

199
00:27:42.300 --> 00:27:46.200
I saw those cards on the way up.
Spades. James. Every one.

200
00:27:46.400 --> 00:27:48.700
You were nailed the minute you left 74.

201
00:27:48.900 --> 00:27:52.500
Only one man can pull together
that much black muscle in this town.

202
00:27:52.700 --> 00:27:54.500
Calls himself Mr Big.

203
00:27:54.700 --> 00:27:58.300
You name the business.
They say he has a black concession.

204
00:28:04.500 --> 00:28:07.200
What would a foreign prime minister
like Kananga

205
00:28:07.400 --> 00:28:09.400
want with an American gangster?

206
00:28:09.600 --> 00:28:13.300
Question is. what would Mr Big
want with a two-bit island diplomat?

207
00:28:13.500 --> 00:28:18.300
Mr Big? Where the hell
does he fit into this mess?

208
00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:24.800
A genuine Felix lighter. Illuminating.

209
00:28:24.900 --> 00:28:26.700
Now listen. James.

210
00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:31.700
Kananga's got a private plane and he's
leaving for San Monique within the hour.

211
00:28:31.900 --> 00:28:35.400
- Get me on the next available flight.
- I already did.

212
00:28:35.600 --> 00:28:40.200
I knew you wouldn't pass up a chance
to get away from where the real action is.

213
00:28:50.900 --> 00:28:53.600
The legendary Baron Samedi. folks.

214
00:28:53.700 --> 00:28:56.400
That's Saturday.
for those who speak French.

215
00:28:56.500 --> 00:28:59.900
Voodoo god of cemeteries
and chief of the legion of the dead.

216
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:03.400
The man who cannot die.
But. for our purposes.

217
00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:07.900
just a performer in a musical
extravaganza we've cooked up

218
00:29:08.100 --> 00:29:10.100
for you wonderful people.

219
00:29:22.300 --> 00:29:25.400
Good evening. The name's Bond.
I have a reservation.

220
00:29:25.600 --> 00:29:29.300
Mr Bond. Of course.
Mrs Bond's been expecting you.

221
00:29:31.500 --> 00:29:34.600
- Mrs Bond?
- She arrived earlier this afternoon.

222
00:29:34.700 --> 00:29:38.700
Said she preferred
something a little more... private.

223
00:29:38.900 --> 00:29:39.900
Bungalow 12.

224
00:29:40.100 --> 00:29:42.600
An incurable romantic - Mrs Bond.

225
00:31:37.100 --> 00:31:39.100
Room service. please.

226
00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:45.400
Room service?
This is Mr Bond. Bungalow 12.

227
00:31:45.600 --> 00:31:49.700
I'd like a bottle of Bollinger. please.
Slightly chilled.

228
00:31:52.600 --> 00:31:55.000
Two glasses. Thank you.

229
00:32:41.100 --> 00:32:43.100
Room service. please.

230
00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:49.400
Room service?
This is Mr Bond. Bungalow 12.

231
00:32:49.600 --> 00:32:53.700
I'd like a bottle of Bollinger. please.
Slightly chilled.

232
00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:59.000
Two glasses. Thank you.

233
00:34:10.800 --> 00:34:12.900
Anybody home?

234
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:22.100
Your champagne. sir.

235
00:34:22.200 --> 00:34:24.500
- What was that?
- Your champagne.

236
00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:26.800
Put it on the table. thanks.

237
00:34:31.700 --> 00:34:34.000
- Shall I open it?
- What?

238
00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:37.000
Shall I open it?

239
00:34:37.600 --> 00:34:40.100
Oh. no. I can manage. Thank you.

240
00:34:42.500 --> 00:34:45.200
- Here you are.
- Thank you.

241
00:36:12.100 --> 00:36:14.800
Mrs Bond. I presume?

242
00:36:15.900 --> 00:36:17.900
I'm Rosie Carver.

243
00:36:21.200 --> 00:36:24.000
I guess I have a little explaining to do.

244
00:36:29.500 --> 00:36:32.200
Yes. Either you or

245
00:36:32.500 --> 00:36:34.700
dear Uncle Felix.

246
00:36:36.400 --> 00:36:38.800
Custom 38. Smith & Wesson.

247
00:36:39.300 --> 00:36:43.800
Corrugated three-inch stock.
no serial number. standard CIA issue.

248
00:36:43.900 --> 00:36:47.300
The question is: why point it at me?

249
00:36:47.400 --> 00:36:51.600
The man who delivered your champagne
is not a hotel waiter.

250
00:36:51.700 --> 00:36:53.600
I was just trying to be careful.

251
00:36:53.800 --> 00:36:56.700
As for Felix Leiter. you're right.

252
00:36:56.900 --> 00:36:59.600
I've worked for CIA down here
for some time now.

253
00:36:59.700 --> 00:37:03.600
He cabled me you were coming
and asked if I would help out if I could.

254
00:37:03.800 --> 00:37:07.300
Perhaps you'd better start
by getting your head together.

255
00:37:09.900 --> 00:37:12.800
- There's a mirror in the bathroom.
- Yes.

256
00:37:13.800 --> 00:37:16.500
You're only my second mission.
you know.

257
00:37:16.600 --> 00:37:19.400
My first was Baines.
The agent who was killed.

258
00:37:20.500 --> 00:37:24.300
It's a relief to know I'm next in line
for the same kind of aid.

259
00:37:31.600 --> 00:37:35.000
- There's a...
- A snake! I should have told you.

260
00:37:35.200 --> 00:37:38.200
You should never go in there
without a mongoose.

261
00:37:38.400 --> 00:37:41.400
I should have never
gotten into any of this!

262
00:37:41.600 --> 00:37:44.400
I'm going to be completely useless to you.

263
00:37:44.600 --> 00:37:47.600
I'm sure we'll be able
to lick you into shape.

264
00:37:48.700 --> 00:37:51.900
It's... getting late. Mrs Bond.

265
00:37:52.000 --> 00:37:54.000
Tomorrow will be a very busy day.

266
00:37:54.200 --> 00:37:57.400
You see. Kananga is
protecting something down here.

267
00:37:57.600 --> 00:38:00.700
Something which Baines
obviously discovered.

268
00:38:00.900 --> 00:38:05.100
You're going to show me the spot
where Baines' body was found.

269
00:38:05.300 --> 00:38:08.800
That. I'm afraid.
only leaves us tonight to...

270
00:38:09.800 --> 00:38:11.800
catch up on old times.

271
00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:15.700
Felix told me there'd be
moments like this.

272
00:38:16.800 --> 00:38:19.500
What did good old Felix suggest?

273
00:38:20.600 --> 00:38:22.400
If all else failed.

274
00:38:22.600 --> 00:38:24.400
cyanide pills.

275
00:38:26.600 --> 00:38:29.100
I settled for two bedrooms.

276
00:38:31.800 --> 00:38:34.000
Good night. Mr Bond.

277
00:38:34.200 --> 00:38:36.300
Mrs Bond.

278
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.800
It's just a hat. darling.

279
00:38:52.000 --> 00:38:55.800
belonging to a small-headed man
who lost a fight with a chicken.

280
00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:58.700
It's a warning. Get it outta here!

281
00:39:00.600 --> 00:39:02.300
Oh. please!

282
00:39:02.800 --> 00:39:05.200
Please don't leave me alone tonight.

283
00:39:05.700 --> 00:39:08.500
James. please promise me!

284
00:39:10.900 --> 00:39:14.400
All right. darling.
if you insist... I promise.

285
00:39:20.700 --> 00:39:22.700
Thank you.

286
00:39:23.600 --> 00:39:25.000
Rosie!

287
00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:28.200
Breakfast's up!

288
00:39:49.700 --> 00:39:51.000
Rosie!

289
00:39:51.200 --> 00:39:53.600
- Are you ready yet?
- What?

290
00:39:53.800 --> 00:39:56.500
I have to see about organising a car.

291
00:39:57.600 --> 00:40:00.100
I'll see you in the lobby.

292
00:40:12.500 --> 00:40:16.600
Over here. sir!
Guarantee big fish. Catch big fish. sir!

293
00:40:16.800 --> 00:40:18.800
Hey. baby! Over here!

294
00:40:18.900 --> 00:40:21.900
Bring your man over here!
Just $20! Have a date!

295
00:40:22.100 --> 00:40:25.100
You got warm lady?
We got cold beer over here. man.

296
00:40:25.200 --> 00:40:28.700
You wanna catch a big fish. sir?
It's only £2 over here.

297
00:40:33.300 --> 00:40:34.900
Good morning.

298
00:40:35.100 --> 00:40:37.800
Come on. Rosie.
This one seems eager enough.

299
00:40:45.200 --> 00:40:46.700
Excuse me!

300
00:40:46.900 --> 00:40:49.000
Where can I change?

301
00:40:51.900 --> 00:40:55.100
Me... clothes off... where?

302
00:41:36.300 --> 00:41:38.700
Stop right there.

303
00:41:39.500 --> 00:41:41.500
Turn around slowly.

304
00:41:43.400 --> 00:41:45.600
Keep your hands up!

305
00:41:46.900 --> 00:41:49.200
As I was saying. Quarrel. a lousy agent.

306
00:41:49.400 --> 00:41:52.000
But the compensations
speak for themselves.

307
00:41:52.100 --> 00:41:55.500
Rosie Carver. meet the man
who shares my hairbrush.

308
00:41:55.700 --> 00:41:57.900
Quarrel Junior.

309
00:41:58.000 --> 00:42:01.200
I'm really sorry. I could have shot you.

310
00:42:02.300 --> 00:42:06.400
You might have even killed me
if you'd taken off the safety catch.

311
00:42:13.800 --> 00:42:15.400
Never mind. darling.

312
00:42:15.500 --> 00:42:19.700
You just let us know when we get
to the spot where Baines was killed.

313
00:42:21.500 --> 00:42:26.100
It's up in the hills.
just after we clear the next cove.

314
00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:40.300
Hey. Quarrel!
Who the hell lives up there?

315
00:42:40.400 --> 00:42:43.000
That's the house of the Kananga woman.

316
00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:46.000
She's supposed to have
the power of the obeah.

317
00:42:46.100 --> 00:42:49.500
No one on the island
dare go up there except him.

318
00:42:56.300 --> 00:42:57.800
He comes again.

319
00:42:58.300 --> 00:43:01.300
There will be violence.

320
00:43:01.500 --> 00:43:03.600
He approaches even now.

321
00:43:03.700 --> 00:43:05.300
By land or water?

322
00:43:05.400 --> 00:43:06.900
Water.

323
00:43:17.000 --> 00:43:18.500
He has arrived.

324
00:43:19.600 --> 00:43:20.800
Good.

325
00:43:20.900 --> 00:43:24.000
Rosie's been more efficient
than I anticipated.

326
00:43:24.900 --> 00:43:27.400
I know where
we could rustle up a car.

327
00:43:27.500 --> 00:43:30.500
Beautiful. brave. and now resourceful.

328
00:43:30.700 --> 00:43:34.000
Rosie. you seem to be staging
a remarkable comeback.

329
00:43:35.800 --> 00:43:37.100
Tell me about the future.

330
00:43:50.800 --> 00:43:52.200
Is it death?

331
00:43:54.500 --> 00:43:56.800
I said. is it death?

332
00:43:56.900 --> 00:43:58.600
It is death.

333
00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:04.700
They're coming.

334
00:44:05.400 --> 00:44:07.400
Rosie knows what to do.

335
00:44:07.500 --> 00:44:10.700
Now. I want no bodies this time. No trace.

336
00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:16.800
It's down there.

337
00:44:18.000 --> 00:44:22.000
But... I thought you said
Baines was killed up in the hills. darling.

338
00:44:24.600 --> 00:44:26.400
Up in the hills. down there.

339
00:44:28.300 --> 00:44:32.200
Why don't we have a bite of lunch
and discuss it?

340
00:44:32.300 --> 00:44:34.900
There's an excellent pâté in the hamper.

341
00:44:35.800 --> 00:44:37.500
I'm in no hurry.

342
00:44:37.700 --> 00:44:39.400
Are you?

343
00:44:41.700 --> 00:44:43.200
No.

344
00:45:05.900 --> 00:45:07.900
James!

345
00:45:08.100 --> 00:45:11.900
You don't know
what finding you has meant to me.

346
00:45:12.100 --> 00:45:13.700
I can imagine.

347
00:45:13.800 --> 00:45:17.100
And you've no idea
what finding this has meant to me.

348
00:45:18.100 --> 00:45:22.100
You do know what the Queen of Cups
means in an upside-down position?

349
00:45:22.300 --> 00:45:25.600
A deceitful. perverse woman.
A liar. a cheat.

350
00:45:25.800 --> 00:45:28.000
And I'd like some answers now.

351
00:45:28.200 --> 00:45:30.100
Please...

352
00:45:30.200 --> 00:45:33.500
You don't understand. sir.
They'll kill me if I do.

353
00:45:33.700 --> 00:45:36.100
And I'll kill you if you don't.

354
00:45:38.500 --> 00:45:43.200
But you couldn't. You wouldn't.
Not after what we've just done.

355
00:45:43.300 --> 00:45:46.200
I certainly wouldn't
have killed you before.

356
00:45:57.800 --> 00:46:02.200
It used to be a convincing act. Rosie.
It's wearing a little thin now.

357
00:46:02.400 --> 00:46:04.800
It's not an act. It's...

358
00:46:05.900 --> 00:46:07.900
Make your choice.

359
00:46:17.600 --> 00:46:19.100
Rosie!

360
00:46:55.200 --> 00:46:57.600
You will explain what went wrong.

361
00:47:00.500 --> 00:47:02.600
I see the intervention of a woman.

362
00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:06.900
The girl was about to confess.
We had to kill her.

363
00:47:09.000 --> 00:47:11.000
The trap was set.

364
00:47:12.400 --> 00:47:14.400
Tee Hee was waiting.

365
00:47:16.000 --> 00:47:18.000
And you saw death.

366
00:47:18.100 --> 00:47:20.600
It must have been the girl's death.

367
00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:24.600
If you do not ask specific questions.

368
00:47:24.800 --> 00:47:29.400
I cannot be responsible for your
misinterpretation of the answers.

369
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:35.000
These growing signs of impertinence
begin to disturb me. Solitaire.

370
00:47:35.200 --> 00:47:37.600
As they did with your mother before you.

371
00:47:37.800 --> 00:47:41.000
She had the power and lost it.
Became useless to me.

372
00:47:41.100 --> 00:47:43.800
You will not make the same mistake.

373
00:47:44.000 --> 00:47:46.000
Solitaire.

374
00:47:48.900 --> 00:47:50.400
Where is Bond now?

375
00:48:14.200 --> 00:48:15.800
Where is Bond now?!

376
00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:21.600
I cannot see
when you are this way with me.

377
00:48:23.200 --> 00:48:25.300
Things become unclear.

378
00:48:25.500 --> 00:48:29.300
Let us hope these momentary lapses
do not become a habit.

379
00:48:29.400 --> 00:48:33.700
Your power exists to serve me.
And it is mine to control.

380
00:48:33.800 --> 00:48:39.400
If and when the time comes I decide you
are to lose it. I myself will take it away.

381
00:48:45.600 --> 00:48:50.800
Solitaire. go to sleep. You have made me
angry with you. and I have no wish to be.

382
00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:52.400
Tee Hee...

383
00:50:11.100 --> 00:50:14.200
Put down those cards!

384
00:50:16.500 --> 00:50:18.600
It is a blasphemy!

385
00:50:19.400 --> 00:50:22.100
They tell nothing
to those who cannot see.

386
00:50:22.200 --> 00:50:25.200
But they do. That's a... a bit of luck.

387
00:50:25.300 --> 00:50:27.200
Good luck. for both of us.

388
00:50:27.400 --> 00:50:30.500
The cards say we will be lovers.

389
00:50:34.500 --> 00:50:36.500
You are mistaken.

390
00:50:36.700 --> 00:50:39.100
It's impossible. Forbidden for me.

391
00:50:40.300 --> 00:50:41.700
Now you must go.

392
00:50:42.300 --> 00:50:44.600
But you do believe....

393
00:50:45.600 --> 00:50:48.200
I mean really believe in the cards?

394
00:50:49.700 --> 00:50:51.900
They have never lied to me.

395
00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:55.600
Then they won't now.

396
00:50:59.600 --> 00:51:01.000
Pick one.

397
00:51:29.400 --> 00:51:32.000
You knew the answer before it was given.

398
00:51:35.100 --> 00:51:37.300
Strangely enough. somehow....

399
00:51:38.000 --> 00:51:39.600
so did l.

400
00:52:14.100 --> 00:52:16.200
So it's finally happened.

401
00:52:17.900 --> 00:52:22.200
Just as it did to my mother...
and her mother before her.

402
00:52:24.700 --> 00:52:26.800
Of course it did.

403
00:52:27.700 --> 00:52:31.000
You're visual proof of that. aren't you?

404
00:52:34.700 --> 00:52:36.800
Come on. cheer up. darling.

405
00:52:38.100 --> 00:52:40.800
There has to be a first time for everyone.

406
00:52:42.500 --> 00:52:44.500
Now tell me.

407
00:52:44.600 --> 00:52:46.600
where's Kananga?

408
00:52:48.400 --> 00:52:50.400
I cannot see.

409
00:52:53.500 --> 00:52:56.400
- Oh. yes. the cards. I'll get them.
- No!

410
00:52:57.900 --> 00:53:00.100
There's no need to be frightened.

411
00:53:01.000 --> 00:53:03.500
You'll soon be rid of him. I promise.

412
00:53:04.700 --> 00:53:06.200
I promise.

413
00:53:08.000 --> 00:53:09.600
I just need a

414
00:53:10.300 --> 00:53:13.400
little bit of information. that's all.

415
00:53:15.000 --> 00:53:16.700
The power...

416
00:53:18.400 --> 00:53:20.100
I've lost it.

417
00:53:23.000 --> 00:53:28.000
The High Priestess is wife
to the Prince no longer of this world.

418
00:53:29.500 --> 00:53:32.900
The spiritual bridge to the secret church.

419
00:53:35.500 --> 00:53:37.600
It was my fate.

420
00:53:37.800 --> 00:53:40.600
By compelling me to earthly love.

421
00:53:40.800 --> 00:53:44.500
the cards themselves
have taken away my powers.

422
00:53:47.500 --> 00:53:49.500
Darling. I've...

423
00:53:49.700 --> 00:53:51.700
a small confession to make.

424
00:53:51.900 --> 00:53:54.200
Now. try not to be too upset.

425
00:53:56.000 --> 00:53:59.300
The deck was slightly stacked
in my favour.

426
00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:01.700
It makes no difference.

427
00:54:01.900 --> 00:54:05.600
The physical violation cannot be undone.

428
00:54:07.800 --> 00:54:10.300
When he finds out I've lost my power....

429
00:54:11.900 --> 00:54:13.600
he'll kill me.

430
00:54:13.800 --> 00:54:16.800
Oh. now. come on.
He'll have to find you first.

431
00:54:17.000 --> 00:54:20.000
Lovers' lesson number one:
we have no secrets.

432
00:54:21.100 --> 00:54:23.600
For example. I have a boat waiting.

433
00:54:23.800 --> 00:54:25.900
You can be on it.

434
00:54:26.800 --> 00:54:32.400
All I have to know before we leave is...
what goes on back there in voodoo land.

435
00:54:34.900 --> 00:54:38.600
Darling. three men and a girl
have been killed in the last four days.

436
00:54:38.700 --> 00:54:41.400
Not counting the times
they've tried to stop me

437
00:54:41.500 --> 00:54:44.300
from discovering
what Kananga's protecting.

438
00:54:44.400 --> 00:54:46.700
Now. do you want to be
on that boat or not?

439
00:54:46.800 --> 00:54:49.700
I simply read the cards for him.

440
00:54:49.800 --> 00:54:52.100
I have never been there.

441
00:54:52.300 --> 00:54:54.600
and he's never taken me there.

442
00:55:05.100 --> 00:55:07.100
I've never dared to go.

443
00:55:07.200 --> 00:55:09.600
But I've looked in the cards.

444
00:55:09.700 --> 00:55:11.900
I've seen great riches there.

445
00:55:13.700 --> 00:55:15.400
They'll kill you.

446
00:55:16.900 --> 00:55:18.600
Us. darling.

447
00:55:19.100 --> 00:55:21.200
They will kill us.

448
00:55:21.300 --> 00:55:24.800
Lovers' lesson number two: togetherness.

449
00:55:25.000 --> 00:55:27.400
Till death do us part. or thereabouts.

450
00:55:28.500 --> 00:55:30.500
Is there time before we leave

451
00:55:31.500 --> 00:55:33.500
for lesson number three?

452
00:55:39.400 --> 00:55:41.000
Absolutely.

453
00:55:41.100 --> 00:55:44.000
There's no sense in going off half-cocked.

454
00:55:57.800 --> 00:56:00.500
- This way.
- How can you be so sure?

455
00:56:00.600 --> 00:56:04.600
These scarecrows are to scare
people away. You're not scared. are you?

456
00:56:04.800 --> 00:56:07.300
Lesson number four:
follow the scarecrows.

457
00:56:42.700 --> 00:56:44.900
- Good morning. boss.
- Morning.

458
00:56:45.100 --> 00:56:48.500
It's sure gonna be a beautiful day.

459
00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:53.100
Yes. sir. a beautiful day!

460
00:57:04.500 --> 00:57:06.900
They're heading for the hill.

461
00:57:09.700 --> 00:57:10.900
They're here.

462
00:57:15.000 --> 00:57:17.100
If he finds it. kill him.

463
00:58:21.900 --> 00:58:23.400
Quick!

464
00:58:34.200 --> 00:58:37.400
We've lost him. He has the girl.

465
00:58:47.200 --> 00:58:50.000
They're somewhere under the nets.

466
00:58:55.600 --> 00:58:59.900
At any cost - any - Bond must die.

467
00:59:19.900 --> 00:59:22.300
Unit 2-5. We have picked them up.

468
00:59:31.600 --> 00:59:37.000
Base to 2-5. Arrest Bond.
But I repeat. the girl is not to be touched.

469
00:59:37.100 --> 00:59:40.200
Message received and understood.
Over and out.

470
00:59:40.400 --> 00:59:45.200
Base to all units.
I repeat. the girl is not to be touched.

471
01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:23.000
Get out of the way!

472
01:02:21.700 --> 01:02:23.700
Sweet mother of pearl!

473
01:02:23.900 --> 01:02:25.400
All change! End of the line!

474
01:02:26.800 --> 01:02:28.400
Get down below. quickly!

475
01:02:28.600 --> 01:02:31.000
Here. I'll do that. You get her started.

476
01:02:39.900 --> 01:02:41.300
It appears... a bus.

477
01:02:48.100 --> 01:02:50.100
James!

478
01:02:51.000 --> 01:02:54.100
He'll be looking for me now.
I know he'll never stop.

479
01:02:54.200 --> 01:02:55.600
Come on. darling.

480
01:02:56.500 --> 01:02:58.300
It's all over.

481
01:03:00.900 --> 01:03:03.500
Voodoo land was just poppy fields.

482
01:03:03.700 --> 01:03:06.100
A simple matter of heroin smuggling.

483
01:03:06.300 --> 01:03:08.800
I'll have a word with a man named Felix.

484
01:03:09.000 --> 01:03:11.700
turn the case over to him.
and you and I will be off.

485
01:03:11.800 --> 01:03:14.500
By the way. where would you like to go?

486
01:03:16.100 --> 01:03:19.300
Anywhere where we can find
one of these.

487
01:03:30.100 --> 01:03:32.200
How quickly can we make it
to New Orleans?

488
01:03:32.400 --> 01:03:34.400
Santa Mina. four hours away...

489
01:03:34.600 --> 01:03:37.500
You could catch a flight
and be there in the morning.

490
01:03:37.700 --> 01:03:42.700
Get in touch with Felix. Tell him to meet
me there tomorrow. Royal Orleans Hotel.

491
01:03:42.800 --> 01:03:44.600
Tampa is closer.

492
01:03:44.800 --> 01:03:49.200
Hamilton was killed in New Orleans.
so there has to be a connection.

493
01:03:49.300 --> 01:03:53.100
And this is a valuable piece
of merchandise we're carrying.

494
01:03:53.200 --> 01:03:55.700
Which. with any luck. they'll want back.

495
01:04:09.700 --> 01:04:11.900
Royal Orleans Hotel. please.

496
01:04:25.200 --> 01:04:27.700
Are you sure this is the way
to New Orleans?

497
01:04:27.800 --> 01:04:32.300
I don't know. but this sure
beats the hell out of Harlem. don't it?

498
01:04:37.100 --> 01:04:39.100
Well. hello. Jim!

499
01:04:39.200 --> 01:04:41.400
What's happenin'. baby?

500
01:04:44.200 --> 01:04:48.100
Just ease back now. Jim. Relax!

501
01:04:48.300 --> 01:04:50.700
Mr Big wants to see you.

502
01:05:16.100 --> 01:05:18.800
You made a mistake
back on that island. Bond.

503
01:05:19.000 --> 01:05:23.300
You took something that didn't belong
to you. from a friend of Mr Big's.

504
01:05:23.400 --> 01:05:27.000
That type of mistake
is tough to bounce back from.

505
01:05:29.300 --> 01:05:32.700
- But I've only just arrived.
- Today is your lucky day. Jim!

506
01:05:32.900 --> 01:05:34.400
You're going skydiving!

507
01:05:34.600 --> 01:05:38.200
There's a helluva view of the lake
from 10.000 feet.

508
01:05:38.400 --> 01:05:41.200
My only regret is I won't be there to see it.

509
01:05:48.200 --> 01:05:49.500
Let's go!

510
01:06:05.900 --> 01:06:07.900
- Good morning. You're...
- Mrs Bell.

511
01:06:08.100 --> 01:06:10.800
You're not my instructor.
Where's Mr Bleeker?

512
01:06:11.000 --> 01:06:13.600
Indisposed. I'll be giving the lesson.

513
01:06:20.500 --> 01:06:22.000
What's on for today?

514
01:06:22.200 --> 01:06:24.500
Let's just wing it. shall we. Mrs Bell?

515
01:06:57.800 --> 01:06:59.400
You're over-revving.

516
01:07:05.000 --> 01:07:08.500
- Leroy. slow down. for Pete's sake!
- Do what the man say!

517
01:07:08.700 --> 01:07:10.700
I can't... I can't find the brake!

518
01:07:21.800 --> 01:07:23.900
Close those doors!

519
01:07:27.000 --> 01:07:28.500
Holy shit!

520
01:07:47.300 --> 01:07:51.100
OK. Don. Don't worry.
I'll take care of it. Right.

521
01:07:51.200 --> 01:07:54.300
Talk to you later.
I've got to go and give a lesson.

522
01:07:59.400 --> 01:08:01.600
Same time tomorrow. Mrs Bell?

523
01:08:02.900 --> 01:08:04.800
Yes. Mr Bleeker.

524
01:08:05.000 --> 01:08:09.300
Yes. sir. I know you just can't
glue the wings back on.

525
01:08:09.400 --> 01:08:13.200
Now. Mr Bleeker. I'm sure
there's no reason for name-calling.

526
01:08:13.400 --> 01:08:16.400
That's fine. Don't forget the double vents.

527
01:08:16.500 --> 01:08:19.400
I appreciate she's one of your best pupils.

528
01:08:19.600 --> 01:08:22.500
That's a little frantic.
I'll keep the other three.

529
01:08:22.700 --> 01:08:26.000
Any such suggestion
should be put in writing to Washington.

530
01:08:26.200 --> 01:08:29.600
- How is Mrs Bell?
- Intensive care. but she'll pull through.

531
01:08:29.700 --> 01:08:32.800
Yes. sir.
No one's questioning your patriotism.

532
01:08:33.000 --> 01:08:35.000
I'm sure you're a veteran. sir.

533
01:08:35.100 --> 01:08:38.700
Felix. find out if there's
a Fillet Of Soul restaurant in town.

534
01:08:38.800 --> 01:08:43.100
We're way ahead of you. It's on
Docker Street. Strutter's watching it now.

535
01:09:47.100 --> 01:09:49.100
Hell of a send-off.

536
01:09:49.300 --> 01:09:50.700
This way.

537
01:10:07.500 --> 01:10:10.800
- Where's Strutter?
- He's gotta be inside somewhere.

538
01:10:14.700 --> 01:10:16.700
Two. gentlemen?

539
01:10:18.400 --> 01:10:21.600
I got a nice booth over here.
just against the wall.

540
01:10:22.400 --> 01:10:26.300
Do you think you could find something
a little closer to the stage?

541
01:10:26.500 --> 01:10:30.400
- What's wrong with a booth?
- I once had a nasty turn in a booth.

542
01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:40.800
- Bourbon. No ice. please.
- Two Sazeracs.

543
01:10:40.900 --> 01:10:44.800
Where's your sense of adventure?
This is New Orleans. Relax!

544
01:10:56.500 --> 01:10:58.800
- One of you Felix Leiter?
- Yeah. right here.

545
01:10:59.000 --> 01:11:01.600
- Call for you. A guy called Strutter.
- Thanks.

546
01:11:01.800 --> 01:11:05.200
For a minute. I thought Harry
was laying down on a job.

547
01:11:38.700 --> 01:11:40.600
What happened to my...

548
01:11:40.800 --> 01:11:44.000
- What happened to my friend?
- What happened? Listen.

549
01:11:46.000 --> 01:11:48.400
Thanks for droppin' in. baby.

550
01:11:48.500 --> 01:11:52.000
Yeah. you're one tough pig to nail down.

551
01:11:53.200 --> 01:11:56.300
You've been picking at me
like some kind of maggot.

552
01:11:56.500 --> 01:11:59.600
First. you go up to Harlem
and kill one of the brothers.

553
01:11:59.700 --> 01:12:01.700
And that disturbed me.

554
01:12:01.800 --> 01:12:05.200
And then you go and steal
this valuable young lady

555
01:12:05.300 --> 01:12:07.700
from my good friend. Dr Kananga.

556
01:12:07.900 --> 01:12:11.700
Now. old Kananga. he believes
in all that card crap.

557
01:12:11.900 --> 01:12:13.500
I mean. he's mad.

558
01:12:13.600 --> 01:12:16.800
Well. possession being
nine points of the law.

559
01:12:17.000 --> 01:12:19.600
I would say Kananga
is your problem now.

560
01:12:19.700 --> 01:12:21.200
Thank you.

561
01:12:21.800 --> 01:12:25.200
In fact. if I were you.
I'd... watch my step from now on.

562
01:12:27.200 --> 01:12:31.100
Yeah. well. you just let me handle
our business with the man.

563
01:12:35.700 --> 01:12:38.500
I got my own plans for you. baby.

564
01:12:40.900 --> 01:12:42.800
But first

565
01:12:43.000 --> 01:12:45.000
there's one little question

566
01:12:45.100 --> 01:12:47.000
that he wants answers for.

567
01:12:47.100 --> 01:12:51.300
Then you'd better ship me back
to the island and let him ask in person.

568
01:12:51.400 --> 01:12:54.400
I'm not in the habit
of giving answers to lackeys.

569
01:12:54.600 --> 01:12:58.600
You damn lucky you got an ear left
to hear the question with.

570
01:12:58.700 --> 01:13:01.600
Which is... did you mess with that?

571
01:13:06.500 --> 01:13:11.500
That's between Solitaire and myself...
and Kananga. I'll tell him when I see him.

572
01:13:11.700 --> 01:13:13.800
You won't see sunlight
unless you answer!

573
01:13:14.000 --> 01:13:16.200
I'd no idea you were so frightened of him.

574
01:13:16.400 --> 01:13:18.000
Did you touch her?!

575
01:13:18.100 --> 01:13:21.000
When I see Kananga.

576
01:13:22.000 --> 01:13:23.500
Right.

577
01:13:44.500 --> 01:13:46.100
Quite revealing.

578
01:13:49.300 --> 01:13:52.400
Kananga: poppy grower
in thousands of acres

579
01:13:52.500 --> 01:13:54.600
of well-camouflaged fields.

580
01:13:54.800 --> 01:13:58.200
protected by the voodoo threat
of Baron Samedi.

581
01:13:58.800 --> 01:14:00.400
Then there's Mr Big.

582
01:14:00.600 --> 01:14:04.800
distributor and wholesaler through
a chain of Fillet Of Soul restaurants.

583
01:14:05.000 --> 01:14:06.700
Wholesale?

584
01:14:08.700 --> 01:14:10.800
Sell heroin. for money?!

585
01:14:10.900 --> 01:14:13.700
My apologies. I'm sure
you simply give it away.

586
01:14:14.300 --> 01:14:16.100
Excellent. Mr Bond.

587
01:14:17.100 --> 01:14:19.700
That's precisely what I intend to do.

588
01:14:19.900 --> 01:14:21.500
Two tons of it. to be exact.

589
01:14:21.600 --> 01:14:24.900
When entering into
a fiercely competitive field.

590
01:14:25.000 --> 01:14:27.900
one finds it advisable
to give away free samples.

591
01:14:28.000 --> 01:14:30.800
Man or woman. black or white.
I don't discriminate.

592
01:14:32.900 --> 01:14:37.000
Two tons of heroin with a street value
well over a billion dollars

593
01:14:37.200 --> 01:14:39.400
nationally distributed free?

594
01:14:40.500 --> 01:14:45.300
That should make a certain group of
families rather angry. wouldn't you say?

595
01:14:45.500 --> 01:14:47.000
Angry?

596
01:14:47.100 --> 01:14:49.000
Why. my dear Mr Bond.

597
01:14:49.200 --> 01:14:52.200
it'll positively drive them
out of their minds.

598
01:14:52.300 --> 01:14:56.000
- And subsequently out of the business.
- Quite ingenious.

599
01:14:56.200 --> 01:14:58.500
A sort of junkies' welfare system.

600
01:14:58.600 --> 01:15:03.100
Merely until the number of addicts
in the country has doubled. shall we say?

601
01:15:03.300 --> 01:15:07.100
Then I will market that acreage
you blundered into the other day.

602
01:15:07.200 --> 01:15:12.300
That heroin will be very expensive indeed.
leaving myself and the phone company

603
01:15:12.500 --> 01:15:16.800
the only two going monopolies
in this nation for years to come.

604
01:15:16.900 --> 01:15:20.900
And here I thought it was Solitaire
who did the fortune-telling.

605
01:15:21.100 --> 01:15:24.300
Let's hope for both your sakes
she still can.

606
01:15:26.000 --> 01:15:30.400
The question still stands. Mr Bond.
Asked by the gentleman concerned.

607
01:15:31.500 --> 01:15:33.100
Did you touch her?

608
01:15:34.600 --> 01:15:38.900
Well. it's not the sort of question...
a gentleman answers.

609
01:15:39.000 --> 01:15:44.100
Well. having set the example.
I don't expect Miss Solitaire

610
01:15:44.200 --> 01:15:46.200
to be any less the lady.

611
01:15:51.900 --> 01:15:53.600
By the way.

612
01:15:53.800 --> 01:15:57.900
that's a particularly handsome watch
you're wearing. Mr Bond.

613
01:15:58.000 --> 01:16:01.800
- May I see it. please?
- You'll forgive me if I don't get up.

614
01:16:04.800 --> 01:16:06.400
Butterhook!

615
01:16:18.500 --> 01:16:19.400
Tee Hee.

616
01:16:21.200 --> 01:16:23.500
On the first wrong answer

617
01:16:24.400 --> 01:16:26.200
from Miss Solitaire.

618
01:16:26.400 --> 01:16:29.600
you will snip the little finger
of Mr Bond's right hand.

619
01:16:36.500 --> 01:16:39.200
Starting with the second wrong answer.

620
01:16:40.500 --> 01:16:43.900
you will proceed
to the more... vital areas.

621
01:16:47.500 --> 01:16:48.700
Solitaire.

622
01:16:48.800 --> 01:16:50.800
my dear.

623
01:16:51.000 --> 01:16:54.000
I want you to listen to me very carefully.

624
01:16:58.400 --> 01:17:00.900
On the back of Mr Bond's watch

625
01:17:01.600 --> 01:17:05.600
the registration number: 3-2-6...

626
01:17:06.700 --> 01:17:08.300
6.

627
01:17:14.800 --> 01:17:16.400
Do I speak the truth?

628
01:17:32.700 --> 01:17:34.700
You speak the truth.

629
01:17:53.700 --> 01:17:54.800
Well....

630
01:17:57.200 --> 01:18:00.700
if nothing else.
at least I've laid your fears to rest.

631
01:18:00.900 --> 01:18:05.200
My compliments on a splendid operation.
There is one thing. however. the...

632
01:18:14.200 --> 01:18:15.200
Whisper.

633
01:18:15.700 --> 01:18:17.200
Take him to the farm.

634
01:18:46.900 --> 01:18:48.900
When do we start back?

635
01:18:55.500 --> 01:18:56.900
Soon. Solitaire.

636
01:18:57.100 --> 01:18:58.500
Soon.

637
01:19:11.700 --> 01:19:13.200
Solitaire. why?

638
01:19:14.000 --> 01:19:17.000
I treated you well. You lacked for nothing.

639
01:19:19.600 --> 01:19:21.600
I don't understand what you...

640
01:19:21.800 --> 01:19:24.300
Mr Bond's watch. my dear.

641
01:19:25.000 --> 01:19:26.900
I gave you every break possible.

642
01:19:27.100 --> 01:19:29.800
You had a 50-50 chance.

643
01:19:29.900 --> 01:19:32.400
You weren't even close.

644
01:19:34.200 --> 01:19:36.700
I had no choice.

645
01:19:37.300 --> 01:19:40.500
Please believe me... The cards!

646
01:19:59.900 --> 01:20:03.300
When the time came. I myself
would have given you love.

647
01:20:04.900 --> 01:20:06.400
You knew that.

648
01:20:06.900 --> 01:20:08.500
You knew that!

649
01:20:11.200 --> 01:20:13.700
There's only one proper way
to deal with this.

650
01:20:18.400 --> 01:20:20.500
And one proper time.

651
01:21:29.900 --> 01:21:32.600
The tonnage order is nearly complete.

652
01:21:36.800 --> 01:21:38.600
We move it out tonight.

653
01:21:42.000 --> 01:21:44.000
And I mean tonight!

654
01:21:44.900 --> 01:21:46.300
Mr Bond.

655
01:21:57.800 --> 01:22:00.600
How much do you know
about crocodiles. Bond?

656
01:22:00.800 --> 01:22:04.900
I've... always tried
to keep them at arm's length myself.

657
01:22:06.100 --> 01:22:08.400
Cute little nippers. ain't they?

658
01:22:09.300 --> 01:22:12.900
I don't suppose those potential
overnight bags are orphans.

659
01:22:13.000 --> 01:22:15.700
Oh. no! We have
some moms and dads as well.

660
01:22:20.600 --> 01:22:23.900
In fact. quite a few thousand.

661
01:22:35.800 --> 01:22:39.100
This is the part I like best: feeding time.

662
01:22:39.300 --> 01:22:42.100
I suspect. the highlight of the tour.

663
01:23:01.500 --> 01:23:04.000
Some of these babies
live to be 200 years old.

664
01:23:08.900 --> 01:23:10.800
Look over there.

665
01:23:10.900 --> 01:23:15.200
That's an alligator.
You can always tell by its round nose.

666
01:23:17.500 --> 01:23:20.400
There's old Albert.

667
01:23:20.600 --> 01:23:22.400
He's a croc.

668
01:23:22.600 --> 01:23:26.500
Got careless with him some time back.
and he took my whole arm off.

669
01:23:26.900 --> 01:23:28.500
Well done. Albert!

670
01:23:28.700 --> 01:23:32.200
They'll eat anything. Even each other.

671
01:23:33.600 --> 01:23:37.700
Then again. sometime they can go
a whole year without eating.

672
01:23:38.800 --> 01:23:40.800
I was rather counting on that.

673
01:23:40.900 --> 01:23:44.500
There are two ways
to disable a crocodile. you know.

674
01:23:49.000 --> 01:23:52.800
I... don't suppose you'd care
to share that information with me?

675
01:23:52.900 --> 01:23:57.300
One way is to jam a pencil
into the depression hole behind his eyes.

676
01:23:57.500 --> 01:23:59.300
And the other?

677
01:23:59.400 --> 01:24:02.100
The other's twice as simple.

678
01:24:03.000 --> 01:24:05.300
You just put your hand in his mouth

679
01:24:05.400 --> 01:24:07.400
and pull his teeth out.

680
01:26:53.100 --> 01:26:54.600
Fire!

681
01:27:02.100 --> 01:27:04.100
Evans. get him!

682
01:27:04.200 --> 01:27:07.800
Adam. in the car! Head him off!
Hector. move. damn it!

683
01:27:22.300 --> 01:27:26.400
Bond ripped off one of our boats.
He's headed for the Irish Bayou.

684
01:27:26.600 --> 01:27:28.600
The man that gets him. stays alive!

685
01:27:28.700 --> 01:27:30.400
Now move. you mothers!

686
01:28:38.900 --> 01:28:40.300
Toby.

687
01:28:40.500 --> 01:28:44.900
I got me a regular Ben Hur down here.

688
01:28:45.100 --> 01:28:47.500
Doin' 95. minimum.

689
01:28:47.700 --> 01:28:51.300
- Need any help. JW?
- Hell. no!

690
01:29:29.500 --> 01:29:32.800
You got a set of wheels
that just won't quit. boy!

691
01:29:32.900 --> 01:29:37.200
If they's yours. that is.
You spin around. boy.

692
01:29:37.900 --> 01:29:40.100
Ten fingers on the fender.

693
01:29:43.700 --> 01:29:45.400
Legs apart.

694
01:29:47.900 --> 01:29:52.000
I'm sure this ain't exactly your debut
at this sort of thing.

695
01:29:54.000 --> 01:29:58.500
You picked the wrong parish
to haul ass through. boy.

696
01:29:58.700 --> 01:30:02.900
Nobody cuts and runs
on Sheriff JW Pepper.

697
01:30:03.500 --> 01:30:07.000
And that's him speakin' that. by the bye!

698
01:30:13.600 --> 01:30:15.100
What the...

699
01:30:44.100 --> 01:30:45.500
JW?

700
01:30:45.600 --> 01:30:51.000
Soon as you nail that offendin' vehicle.
Miss Pearson just called.

701
01:30:51.200 --> 01:30:54.500
Seems her dog's
foamin' all at the mouth.

702
01:30:54.700 --> 01:30:57.000
She's got him locked up in the shed

703
01:30:57.200 --> 01:31:00.800
and wondered if you'd like to
come over and shoot it for her.

704
01:31:03.600 --> 01:31:06.400
You tell Miss Pearson to take a flyin'...

705
01:31:08.300 --> 01:31:11.700
That look like a boat stuck
in the Sheriff's car there. Eddie?

706
01:31:11.900 --> 01:31:16.400
Boy. where you been all your life?
That there's one of them new car-boats.

707
01:31:16.500 --> 01:31:20.700
By the powers invested in me
by this parish.

708
01:31:21.700 --> 01:31:27.300
I hereby do commandeer this vehicle
and all those persons within.

709
01:31:29.700 --> 01:31:32.900
And that means you. smart ass!

710
01:32:54.300 --> 01:32:56.100
Unit 23 in position.

711
01:32:56.300 --> 01:32:58.700
Ten-four. 23. Come in. 28.

712
01:32:58.800 --> 01:33:03.300
Hey. JW. Seems like Deke Rogers
done got his boat stole off the river

713
01:33:03.500 --> 01:33:05.900
but got a new one in his swimming pool.

714
01:33:06.100 --> 01:33:09.600
- Sheriff. get your boys off my frequency!
- Give me that!

715
01:33:09.800 --> 01:33:12.000
Now you listen to me. trooper boy!

716
01:33:12.100 --> 01:33:14.700
We got a swamp full of Black Russians

717
01:33:14.900 --> 01:33:18.000
drivin' boats to beat the band down here!

718
01:33:18.200 --> 01:33:22.900
Relax. Sheriff. We've got a roadblock
waiting for them at Miller's Bridge.

719
01:33:23.900 --> 01:33:28.000
Unit 26 at Miller's Bridge.
We're just about all set here.

720
01:33:28.200 --> 01:33:30.800
Make that secure there! D'you hear?

721
01:33:34.200 --> 01:33:36.100
OK. fellas. Here they come!

722
01:33:50.700 --> 01:33:53.300
All right. out of my way!
I'm in charge here!

723
01:33:53.400 --> 01:33:55.400
You two boys. come on!

724
01:34:01.000 --> 01:34:05.100
I want those two men and
their boats apprehended immediately!

725
01:34:05.200 --> 01:34:07.400
Yes. sir. Captain. I understand.

726
01:34:07.600 --> 01:34:11.700
But. I don't know where we're gonna find
a boat fast enough to catch 'em.

727
01:34:11.900 --> 01:34:17.300
Call my brother-in-law. Billy Bob. He's got
the fastest boat on the whole damn river.

728
01:34:17.400 --> 01:34:21.800
Billy Bob'll sure enough fix their ass!
Yeah. call Billy Bob.

729
01:34:28.200 --> 01:34:32.500
There's two boats. Billy Bob.
They're movin' like buttered pigs!

730
01:34:32.700 --> 01:34:36.100
Now. I promised these boys here
you'd get 'em. Don't let me down.

731
01:34:36.300 --> 01:34:38.600
Cool down. JW. I'm on my way.

732
01:34:39.100 --> 01:34:43.000
- Want something. boy?
- Yes. I'd like to borrow this boat. if I may.

733
01:34:43.200 --> 01:34:46.300
Everybody on the river
would like to borrow this boat.

734
01:34:49.100 --> 01:34:55.200
Billy Bob. we've got 'em spotted.
They're headed for Hayley's Landing.

735
01:35:08.500 --> 01:35:11.300
That's my brother-in-law!
That's Billy Bob!

736
01:35:11.500 --> 01:35:13.700
He'll get 'em! Billy Bob'll get 'em!

737
01:35:16.000 --> 01:35:17.500
Hot damn!

738
01:35:17.600 --> 01:35:23.000
If one side of the Pepper family
don't get 'em. the other side will! Let's go!

739
01:36:19.600 --> 01:36:24.500
If any man can show just cause why they
may not lawfully be joined together.

740
01:36:24.600 --> 01:36:27.100
let him now speak. or else hereafter...

741
01:36:50.800 --> 01:36:52.700
Headquarters to all units.

742
01:36:52.900 --> 01:36:56.200
Suspects seen proceeding down
by Liberty towards Highway 11.

743
01:36:56.400 --> 01:36:57.800
Proceed with caution.

744
01:37:01.500 --> 01:37:04.100
Would you get that chicken coop
off the road?!

745
01:37:06.300 --> 01:37:10.100
Did you ever think of gettin'
a driver's license. boy?!

746
01:38:00.300 --> 01:38:04.000
Are you sure that was
your brother-in-law. Sheriff?

747
01:40:17.400 --> 01:40:20.700
- Felix. what are you doing here?
- We'll get to that later.

748
01:40:20.900 --> 01:40:24.200
Kananga's in town. He's got your girl.
They just took off.

749
01:40:27.100 --> 01:40:29.600
There's the son of a bitch! I got him!

750
01:40:33.900 --> 01:40:35.400
What are you?

751
01:40:35.600 --> 01:40:39.500
Some kind of doomsday machine. boy?

752
01:40:39.600 --> 01:40:43.600
Well. we've got a cage strong enough
to hold an animal like you here!

753
01:40:43.800 --> 01:40:47.200
- Captain. enlighten the sheriff. please.
- Yes. sir.

754
01:40:47.300 --> 01:40:49.900
JW. let me have a word with you.

755
01:40:50.800 --> 01:40:53.600
JW. now this fella's
from London. England.

756
01:40:53.700 --> 01:40:57.500
He's an Englishman workin'
in cooperation with our boys.

757
01:40:57.700 --> 01:41:00.800
- A sort of secret agent.
- Secret agent?!

758
01:41:01.700 --> 01:41:04.000
On whose side?!

759
01:41:04.200 --> 01:41:08.900
We busted the Fillet of Soul an hour ago.
We came up with nothing but these.

760
01:41:09.700 --> 01:41:11.500
Kananga's clear.

761
01:41:11.700 --> 01:41:15.000
You should have seen the size
of the guy on the boat with him.

762
01:41:15.200 --> 01:41:16.500
Nine feet tall. I swear.

763
01:41:16.700 --> 01:41:21.400
Big top hat. a cockamamie flute
in one hand and Solitaire in the other.

764
01:41:51.200 --> 01:41:54.100
The incendiary bombs
are set for midnight.

765
01:41:54.300 --> 01:41:57.800
Now. that gives you exactly... 30 minutes.

766
01:42:00.100 --> 01:42:02.300
Watch out for sharks on the way back.

767
01:42:02.500 --> 01:42:04.700
We'll see you for breakfast. Felix.

768
01:42:04.900 --> 01:42:06.600
Good hunting!

769
01:42:23.100 --> 01:42:26.400
You're going to need these
and the shark gun on the way back.

770
01:42:28.800 --> 01:42:30.800
Seems like the party's started.

771
01:42:31.000 --> 01:42:34.800
My regards to Baron Samedi. man -
right between the eyes.

772
01:48:58.300 --> 01:49:00.100
Trouble!

773
01:50:03.700 --> 01:50:06.100
Mr Bond! There you are!

774
01:50:06.200 --> 01:50:07.900
And Miss Solitaire as well.

775
01:50:08.100 --> 01:50:10.200
Hardly unexpected. but most welcome.

776
01:50:10.900 --> 01:50:12.300
Whisper!

777
01:50:12.500 --> 01:50:14.500
Two more glasses for our guests!

778
01:50:15.600 --> 01:50:19.100
- What shall we drink to. Mr Bond?
- How about an earthquake?

779
01:50:29.900 --> 01:50:32.100
Welcome home. Where's our boy?

780
01:50:32.200 --> 01:50:34.200
He'll be along any time now.

781
01:50:34.400 --> 01:50:37.400
I checked behind a rock
and his wet suit is gone.

782
01:50:38.400 --> 01:50:40.400
Keep the change.

783
01:50:43.300 --> 01:50:45.500
It is unfortunate your wet suit was found

784
01:50:45.700 --> 01:50:48.100
only minutes before
the field was destroyed.

785
01:50:48.200 --> 01:50:50.000
Don't tell me you're not insured?

786
01:50:51.200 --> 01:50:53.300
The poppy is a very sturdy flower.

787
01:50:53.500 --> 01:50:56.900
You have been
a relatively minor nuisance. in fact.

788
01:50:57.000 --> 01:51:00.800
But this gun...
I find it particularly fascinating.

789
01:51:00.900 --> 01:51:02.300
What is it?

790
01:51:03.600 --> 01:51:07.100
A shark gun. naturally.
With compressed gas pellets.

791
01:51:30.700 --> 01:51:32.600
Ingenious!

792
01:51:32.800 --> 01:51:34.400
Don't

793
01:51:34.600 --> 01:51:38.000
pull the pin out. The air in here
is foul enough already.

794
01:51:39.800 --> 01:51:42.400
Somehow I never thought of you
as a poor loser.

795
01:51:42.600 --> 01:51:45.600
I was hoping you would join me
to drink to the future.

796
01:51:45.800 --> 01:51:50.900
Miss Solitaire used to know all about
the future. Especially predicting death.

797
01:51:53.900 --> 01:51:55.900
An underground monorail.

798
01:51:58.000 --> 01:52:01.500
Connected to the last refuge
of a scoundrel. no doubt.

799
01:52:02.600 --> 01:52:06.700
The heroin leaves here. I take it.
carried somewhere by that winch.

800
01:52:06.800 --> 01:52:09.800
Correct again. Mr Bond.
What a quick study you are.

801
01:52:10.000 --> 01:52:11.900
Let me show you exactly how it works.

802
01:52:12.000 --> 01:52:14.500
Where in hell can the man be?

803
01:52:14.700 --> 01:52:17.400
Relax!
He must have got tied up somewhere.

804
01:52:18.700 --> 01:52:21.400
These cans hold 25 pounds each.

805
01:52:21.600 --> 01:52:25.300
There are 20 cans to a shipment.
packed in watertight

806
01:52:27.600 --> 01:52:29.700
metal containers.

807
01:52:29.900 --> 01:52:33.900
It's your show. but isn't there
a simpler way of drowning someone?

808
01:52:35.800 --> 01:52:37.800
Drown. Mr Bond?

809
01:52:37.900 --> 01:52:40.100
I doubt you'd get the chance to drown.

810
01:53:16.300 --> 01:53:19.700
Perhaps we could try something
on an even simpler vein.

811
01:53:19.900 --> 01:53:21.900
On the contrary. Mr Bond.

812
01:53:22.800 --> 01:53:25.900
I think you'll find those wounds quite
fatal.

813
01:54:09.400 --> 01:54:11.800
Whisper...

814
01:54:12.800 --> 01:54:14.200
The gate.

815
01:54:17.700 --> 01:54:22.600
Slowly. Whisper. slowly. slowly.
Let our diners assemble.

816
01:55:10.100 --> 01:55:11.700
Look out!

817
01:56:10.300 --> 01:56:11.700
Where's Kananga?

818
01:56:11.900 --> 01:56:14.800
He always did have
an inflated opinion of himself.

819
01:56:21.000 --> 01:56:23.000
Oh. James!

820
01:56:23.700 --> 01:56:25.700
How do we get out of here?

821
01:56:26.400 --> 01:56:27.900
We take the train. of course.

822
01:56:30.500 --> 01:56:34.500
Thanks for everything. Felix.
See you tomorrow night at the 21 Club.

823
01:56:34.700 --> 01:56:36.700
Why do you want to travel this way?

824
01:56:36.800 --> 01:56:40.500
What the hell can the two of you do
on the train for 16 hours?

825
01:56:41.500 --> 01:56:43.800
Say goodbye to Felix. darling.

826
01:56:53.900 --> 01:56:57.200
Now. the first thing to learn
in playing gin rummy

827
01:56:57.400 --> 01:57:01.700
is never take a card from the exposed
pile unless you really need it.

828
01:57:07.200 --> 01:57:08.200
Gin.

829
01:57:13.800 --> 01:57:16.400
James! What are you doing?

830
01:57:19.500 --> 01:57:21.800
Just testing an old adage.

831
01:57:22.000 --> 01:57:24.000
"Unlucky at cards..."

832
01:57:46.300 --> 01:57:49.700
- Do hurry up. James.
- Won't be a moment. darling.

833
01:58:17.600 --> 01:58:21.200
Lock the door as well on your way up.
would you. James?

834
01:58:22.600 --> 01:58:27.500
After all. we wouldn't want anyone
to just walk in on us. would we?

835
01:58:32.900 --> 01:58:37.000
For the first time in my life.
I feel like a complete woman.

836
01:58:38.400 --> 01:58:40.800
The slightest touch of your hand...

837
01:58:41.900 --> 01:58:46.000
I was always so afraid that
a part of me would stay with the past.

838
01:58:46.100 --> 01:58:49.300
But now I know
there's no chance of that any longer.

839
01:58:50.200 --> 01:58:52.600
To be able to reach out and touch you...

840
01:58:55.900 --> 01:58:58.700
Mr Bond. It's good to see you again.

841
02:00:48.600 --> 02:00:50.800
Well. that wasn't very funny!

842
02:00:53.300 --> 02:00:54.700
Now what are you doing?

843
02:00:59.800 --> 02:01:02.300
Just being disarming. darling.
